    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0332" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3425</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Guthrie</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-03T15:00:00+09:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 4, 3.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 1, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d181-f1"/> In an interview with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Japan Advertiser</hi> editor yesterday the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs said that no such proposals had ever been received in Japan from
                    Mexico. He said: <pb facs="0333" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>First, it is absurd to suppose that Japan would under any circumstances
                            desert the Allies and join Germany. In the second place, it is
                            preposterous to imagine that Mexico could induce Japan to follow such a
                            course. This plot shows what mental delusion Germany is laboring under
                            to presume that such a course of [conduct] could ever be possible.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The interview is confirmed by the Foreign Office.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d181-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guthrie</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
